---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { roles } from '../../data/roles';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Solutions by role | Canonical Cloud"
  description="For founders, finance, operations, engineering, sales, and security teams: practical paths to operational visibility and compliance readiness."
>
  <section class="page-hero shell role-index-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Solutions by role</p>
    <h1>The right starting point depends on what you own.</h1>
    <p>Whether you are closing an enterprise deal, making operations repeatable, or turning security gaps into engineering work, start with your team's real responsibility.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="#choose-role">Choose your role</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={site.readinessUrl}>Explore readiness services</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell role-index-section" id="choose-role">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Six ways in</p>
      <h2>Speak to your next decision, not just a framework.</h2>
      <p>These guides are written for the people responsible for outcomes at growing software companies, including seed-stage teams where one person wears multiple hats.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="role-grid">
      {roles.map((role, index) => (
        <a class="role-card" href={`/roles/${role.slug}/`} aria-labelledby={`role-${role.slug}-title`} aria-describedby={`role-${role.slug}-problem`}>
          <span class="role-card-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <h3 id={`role-${role.slug}-title`}>{role.label}</h3>
          <p id={`role-${role.slug}-problem`}>{role.problem}</p>
          <span class="role-card-link" aria-hidden="true">Explore this role →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell role-products">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">One journey, distinct responsibilities</p>
      <h2>Operations and readiness are connected—not interchangeable.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="role-product-grid">
      <article class="role-product">
        <p class="eyebrow">Canonical Cloud</p>
        <h3>The operational foundation</h3>
        <p>Understand cloud services, deployment and CI context, evidence, ownership, and ongoing operational follow-through.</p>
        <a href="/product/">Explore Canonical Cloud →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="role-product">
        <p class="eyebrow">Canonical Plus</p>
        <h3>Readiness and remediation</h3>
        <p>Scope applicable requirements, identify control and evidence gaps, prioritize fixes, and prepare for an independent review.</p>
        <a href={site.readinessUrl}>Explore Canonical Plus →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="role-boundary">Canonical Plus provides readiness support, not audit opinions, certifications, authorizations, or guaranteed approval. Formal decisions remain with qualified independent reviewers and authorities.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="access-section shell role-final-cta">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start with the actual trigger</p>
    <h2>Tell us what the buyer, board, or next milestone requires.</h2>
    <p>A well-scoped readiness discussion begins with the systems, deadlines, and business commitments involved.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button role-light-button" href={site.consultationUrl}>Book a readiness conversation</a>
      <a class="button role-outline-button" href={site.quoteUrl}>Explore an estimate</a>
    </div>
    <p class="role-cta-note">The quote is a non-binding planning estimate. Email delivery may be unavailable; book an intro for follow-up. Do not include credentials or sensitive evidence in a public form.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
